Execute:

```bash id="v8m3wp"
ssh fakeuser@localhost
```

OR

```bash id="q5r9tk"
ssh kali@localhost
```

Enter incorrect passwords multiple times (5–10 attempts).

Observation:

* Authentication fails repeatedly.

---

# Part G: Analyzing Failed Login Attempts

## Step 20: Detect Failed Password Attempts

Execute:

```bash id="t1x7mv"
journalctl | grep "Failed password"
```

Observation:

* Failed SSH login attempts are displayed.

Example:

```text id="g6q2zp"
Failed password for kali from 127.0.0.1 port 53512 ssh2
```

---

## Step 21: Extract Suspicious IP Addresses

Execute:

```bash id="m9v5qd"
journalctl | grep "Failed password" | awk '{print $11}'
```

Observation:

* IP addresses responsible for failed attempts are displayed.

Example:

```text id="r3x8tk"
127.0.0.1
```

---

## Step 22: Count Failed Attempts per IP

Execute:

```bash id="y7m1wp"
journalctl | grep "Failed password" | awk '{print $11}' | sort | uniq -c | sort -nr
```

Observation:

* Failed login attempt counts per IP address are displayed.

Example:

```text id="k2v9qe"
10 127.0.0.1
```

Inference:

* Repeated attempts from same IP indicate brute force behavior.

